# The shrink check reads a `[a]+` parameter as known non-empty, so `Drop xs, 1` is strictly
# smaller than `xs` from the clause's first line (Semantics ch. 7, Keep shrinking; Type
# System ch. 2, "Collections"), and a cast is the value it casts, so the `? rest` of the
# checked cast is no larger than what was dropped from. Written by Claude on the
# claude-bugs branch; subject to change.
Total: fn [Nat]+ -> Nat
fn Total xs = match ((Drop xs, 1) as [Nat]+?):
    nil: Or xs[0], 0
    ? rest: (Or xs[0], 0) + (Total rest)
